    "result": "Perfect! All tests are now passing. Here's what I fixed:\n\n## Issues Found and Fixed\n\n### 1. **Governance module missing exports** (src/finetune/index.js)\nThe test was trying to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only available in the default export. I added an explicit re-export statement:\n```javascript\nexport { APPROVAL_STATUSES, DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS, DEFAULT_GOVERNANCE_TEMPLATE, GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS, RISK_LEVELS };\n```\n\n### 2. **Toxicity metric receiving wrong parameter** (src/eval/metrics.js)\nThe `toxicityMetric` function signature is `toxicityMetric(outputs, bannedTerms)`, but the evaluation harness was passing both outputs and references as arguments. The references were being incorrectly interpreted as banned terms, causing the toxicity score to be 0 instead of 1. I wrapped the metric call to ignore the references:\n```javascript\n(outs, refs) => toxicityMetric(outs)\n```\n\nAll 28 tests now pass across all 8 test files. \u2705",
